; --- BTN-1: the button's parts. Same recipe as the other two rooms' — a shared prefab would be
; the obvious move and is the wrong one here: SupermarketWorldSelfTest compares each room's
; PACKED node count against its LIVE one, and an instanced sub-scene contributes one node to the
; packed side and all of its children to the live side. Authoring the plate in each room keeps
; the check honest AND keeps the rule the check exists for — every part of a level is authored in
; its own scene file, openable in the editor.

